From bc2a5268c604dda8a2bf4c828c8ae36aced99080 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Atlas agent <agent@atlas.local>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:06:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] render_pass: no fatal refusal of an attachment the device
 makes no image of

On 2026-11-14 the VM's QEMU died at renderCommandEncoderWithDescriptor:
with "Unsupported { feature: TextureSize, needs: [[Limit {
MaxImageDimension2D, required: 1024, available: 0 }]] }" (qemu.3.log:590),
just after a 1024x1024 ASTC8x8LDR texture was announced held in a
BC7_UNORM_BLOCK carrier. A color attachment without RenderTarget usage
renders through a stand-in made in its image's format with
COLOR_ATTACHMENT. ANV renders no BC/ETC2/EAC/ASTC/PVRTC carrier and no
E5B9G9R9_UFLOAT_PACK32, so vkGetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties2
answers VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED, Device::image_limits turns that
into limits all 0, and check_image_limits reported a 2D size limit of 0.
Reims aborts on any refusal of that call but nil.

- image_plan::check_image_limits: the all-0 answer (never a supported
  combination's: maxMipLevels and maxArrayLayers are at least 1) is
  refused Format, needing the image's Vulkan format in its first
  attachment, storage or sampled usage, and naming the texture's Metal
  pixel format as its symbol, as every refusal of a format does: Reims
  reads that symbol as a Metal format's name (ycbcr::pass_refused). The
  whole combination (Metal and Vulkan formats, usage, flags, view
  formats, samples, type, VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED) is said on
  stderr where the runtime makes an image (check_made_limits:
  m2v-unmade-image, the first 16, then at powers of two). The format
  answers (families/formats.rs) check without it.
- render_pass::stood_format: a texture without RenderTarget usage of a
  format the device renders through its word (WordAttachment:
  RGB9E5Float, R8/RG8 sRGB, the packed 16-bit ones) renders through a
  stand-in in the word's format, as a render target of the format does.
  Before, RGB9E5Float's pass was refused as above on ANV, and an
  R8Unorm_sRGB one opened but its setRenderPipelineState: was refused
  NotImplemented(Render), also fatal under Reims.
- RenderPassProblem::CompressedColorAttachment: a color attachment of a
  compressed format, which no device renders, is answered nil, naming
  the first such color. The answer comes after the command buffer's
  state (render.rs open_render: a pass with a compressed color is
  refused EncoderOpen or AlreadyCommitted there, as any pass is), after
  every color attachment's own checks (render_pass::check_colors: custom
  sample depth store, resolve, YCbCr, foreign texture, level and slice),
  and before any image of the pass is made. Depth and stencil
  attachments are checked after it, as before. Reims takes a nil encoder
  (NoEncoder), skips the pass and goes on. Each answer is said on stderr
  (m2v-compressed-attachment: the texture and the pass's attachments;
  the first 16, then at powers of two). Basis: unknown, plain Metal's
  answer is unmeasured.

Not a scratch stand-in whose writes are discarded: built and tested, it
opened the pass, but a guest pipeline with a color at that index meets
an attachment of another format at setRenderPipelineState:, refused
AttachmentFormat, and Reims sends that call and every draw with
Policy::Dies (encode_render.rs run). Skipping those calls instead would
be a new mode across every draw, indirect and tile entry point, with no
Metal answer to hold it to. Nil skips the pass whole.

Not known: why the guest attached an ASTC texture there. The stderr line
names the pass the next time it happens.

Tests: tests/image_plan.rs holds the all-0 refusal to the Metal format's
name and its words to the whole combination (no device).
tests/unrenderable_attachments.rs (device, validation layer on) holds:
every worded format without RenderTarget usage to a render target's
bytes through a clear, a load and a draw; hand-computed codes for
R8Unorm_sRGB, RG8Unorm_sRGB, RGB9E5Float and B5G6R5Unorm, unblended and
blended One/Zero; a SourceAlpha blend to the render target's bytes;
every compressed format, at color 0 and 1, loaded, cleared or not, to
nil with its blocks unchanged and the command buffer going on; a
compressed level or slice to nil once its subresource is checked; a
pass with a compressed color to EncoderOpen and AlreadyCommitted as any
pass; a stand-in or compressed color 0 beside a compressed or
out-of-range color 1 to color 1's answer; and every color format to no
refusal naming a limit of 0.
At base 7 of these 8 fail on ANV and on lavapipe, the compressed ones
with the production refusal (ASTC8x8LDR, required 1024, available 0);
the blend one, which compares to the render target's answer, passes.
All 8 pass after on both. An all-format sweep on ANV: 171 refusals of a
limit of 0 before, none after; the other 804 refusals are unchanged.
Runtime lib suites keep their failures apart from flaky ones (no
device: the same 2; lavapipe and the ANV targeted suites: flaky ones,
render_stage_digests and others, vary by run, at base too). The
validation lane's no-RenderTarget color and depth passes still pass on
ANV.
docs/REFUSALS.md is regenerated (its EncoderOpen row was already behind
the code); api_signatures.tsv gains the variant's row only.
